{
  "id": "RECV-AFTER-DISCONNECT",
  "title": "Server processes client messages after the client's DISCONNECT",
  "source": "RFC 4253 §11.1",
  "quote": "This message causes immediate termination of the connection. / The sender MUST NOT send or receive any data after this message, and the recipient MUST NOT accept any data after receiving this message.",
  "level": "MUST",
  "rationale": "The client DISCONNECT is sent from a clean point (before or during the canonical initial KEX, or after it with ordinary traffic) so the server can read it. If the connection stays open and a later input draws any server message other than DISCONNECT, the server accepted data after DISCONNECT. A server that merely lingers silently is not flagged.",
